If you can see this file, then the methods written below turned out to be sufficient.

Problem - can't use github in IntelliJ, namely:
-> Get from Version Control...
-> GitHub
- (account is added but all you can see is)
-> "Invalid authentication data. Re-Login"

How to solve that:
In the same bar as 'File', 'Edit', etc. there is 'Help'. And at the very bottom there is 'About'.
Make sure your current build is newer that June 10, 2024.
Either way, if you want to update, then go to the section 'Help', 'Check for Updates...', and update.
(Windows 10) if you see that 'elevator.exe' needs access to you hard drive, you need to accept it. Only then will the update be installed.
If <now> your version is newer that June 10, 2024, you can progress further.

Further:
Try if you can clone a repository. If you still see the same issue, you may try to re-login by hand (I did that).
Namely, go to 'File' -> 'Settings' -> 'Version Control' -> 'GitHub'. There, remove your account from the list (aka log out).
Now (in 'Get from Version Control...' -> 'GitHub') try to 'Log in via GitHub...'.
If it's insufficient (you only see public repositories, or none), log out again.
In (in 'Get from Version Control...' -> 'GitHub') go to 'Log in with Token...'.
Clicking that 'Generate' option will lead you to the correct site. There, choose what you need and generate the Token.
It's gonna be a random string. You need to paste that just on the left of that 'Generate' button you pressed a second ago.
And now just log in. Default setting of the Token should allow you to see all your repositories now.

